<title>GERMANY: Waigel says delay could kill off EMU.</title>
<headline>Waigel says delay could kill off EMU.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel was quoted on Monday as saying that a delay to Europe's single currency could kill off the project altogether.</p>
<p>&quot;Whoever calls for a five-year delay must know that the project would by then be dead,&quot; Waigel told the &quot;Super Illu&quot; illustrated weekly.</p>
<p>He was responding to calls by Kurt Biedenkopf, premier in the eastern state of Saxony, for a long delay to European economic and monetary union (EMU) to enable would-be members to meet the fiscal criteria to join.</p>
<p>He said that anyone attempting to eliminate the timetable from the EMU debate must know &quot;that consolidation and stability efforts in most countries would come to a standstill.&quot;</p>
</text>
